      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70703,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Intratesticular or paratesticular</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:36:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70704,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The mean patient age is 53&nbsp;years. Patients present with scrotal swelling, sometimes with tenderness.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:36:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70705,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours are very rare, with only 7&nbsp;benign cases and 1&nbsp;malignant case reported {552866; 28123743; 2021324; 3739969}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:36:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70706,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is some evidence that Brenner tumours may originate from Walthard nests, which are common in the tunica vaginalis of the testis, or from mesothelium, because an association with adenomatoid tumour has been observed {421180}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:36:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70707,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:36:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70708,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Brenner tumours are solid and fibromatous, measuring 27&ndash;73&nbsp;mm. A cystic tumour has also been described {28123743}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:36:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70709,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Brenner tumours in the testis or paratestis resemble their counterparts in the ovary. Benign tumours are typically composed of nests of bland urothelial-type cells with elongated grooved nuclei within a fibromatous stroma. Borderline tumours usually exhibit papillary projections of atypical urothelial-type epithelium in cystic spaces without infiltrative growth. Malignant tumours consist of nests of highly atypical urothelial-type epithelium showing invasive growth. Mitoses are frequent. Malignant Brenner tumours are usually associated with a benign or borderline Brenner tumour component. Immunohistochemical studies performed on ovarian Brenner tumours reveal positivity for CK7, GATA3, p63, and uroplakin, and negativity for CK20, PAX8, WT1, ER, and PR {25281026; 22198845}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:36:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70710,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:36:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
